      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are some more jokes that lean into the \"controversial\" side of Italian American and Irish American stereotypes:\n\n1. \"I was at an Italian American birthday party and it was like a human pinball machine – 20 guys, talking, eating, drinking, and at the center of it all was a 50-year-old table flipper. Meanwhile, Irish Americans are like 'Happy St. Patrick's Day, everyone!' and then someone inevitably starts telling that one true story from college to get everyone drunk.\"\n2. \"You know what's interesting about Italian American culture? They're the only group that's allowed to yell at theoyer during a chaotic family dinner, while Irish Americans are just like 'Down's syndrome is literally anyone who says \"trade unionism hurts my wrist'\"\"\n3. \"I went to an Irish American wedding and it was like a 'We're gonna party hard and get married lightly' deal. Meanwhile Italian American weddings are like 'Let's party hard but maybe plan out our culinary symphony first'. Don't get me wrong, but Irish will swallow more Yuengling on their  communion day, than some Wedding Grooms will – recovering work for the feast. Unfortunately vetch kidney jewels benefits surpass too",
